    <GaugingStation location="Dolybont" name="Leri" number="64006">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Crump profile weir in a straight flood-banked reach. Abstractions and discharges affect flow.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">No cableway. Modular limit unknown. Wing walls contain flows to high levels. Suffers from gravel accumulation. Weir was repaired summer 2018. One peak flow rating applied over period of record, which shows good fit to available gaugings.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">A 10m wide single crest Crump profile weir in a straight flood-banked reach.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">The river burst its banks upstream of the station during the record high flow event of 8 June 2012, causing some of the flow to bypass the station. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2019 (WINFAP Files v8) and in August 2025 (WINFAP Files v14).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Abstraction into Craig-y-Pistyll reservoir and five discharges upstream of gauging station; substantial net loss of water resulting from these transfers, since sum of discharges does not nearly equal amount of water withdrawn for reservoir.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Predominantly impervious Silurian rocks. Majority grassland, some forested area.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">S</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Weir and high wingwalls allow extrapolation of rating to QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Few high flow gaugings." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
